# lldb — lift-source

Upstream: https://github.com/conda-forge/lldb-feedstock
Fork:     https://github.com/NAGAGroup/lldb-feedstock
Pinned:   b81da2d5cfaadc78b8997d335a5ff2c5e0ebb9a1 (conda-forge main, 2026-07-21)

LIFT, NOT SUBMODULE: we do not build this feedstock. Its content is copied
into our own core recipe, because acpp forces LLVM+clang into ONE cmake
configure and conda-forge's per-component split cannot carry it.

The debugger. WHAT WE LIFT: build flags, and specifically its python-binding
wiring — the bindings are compiled against whichever python HOST resolved, so
the single `python` pin in variants.yaml is load-bearing here.

SCOPE CORRECTION (Jack, 2026-09-05): acpp-lldb is CORE on EVERY platform,
Windows included. "lldb is absent from Windows' LLVM_ENABLE_PROJECTS" was OUR
build's omission, not upstream's — conda-forge ships lldb on Windows. Two
reasons it must be there: it is a strong debugger Windows users want, and our
run_constraints would otherwise PREVENT a Windows user from getting lldb from
conda-forge at all.

TO DIFF AGAINST UPSTREAM:
    git clone https://github.com/NAGAGroup/lldb-feedstock
    git -C lldb-feedstock diff b81da2d5cfaadc78b8997d335a5ff2c5e0ebb9a1..origin/main
